Tests: added `malformed device params are rejected before permissions or capture`, a 4-case argument test over snap, clip, location.get and screen.record. Camera and microphone are denied, so it checks that params are validated before permissions. With the base `MacNodeRuntime.swift` it fails 4/4 (11 issues): screen.record writes a recording and location.get returns ok. With the fix, `swift test --filter MacNodeRuntimeTests` passes 46 tests, including the existing omitted-params cases (`camera enumeration requires only the OpenClaw toggle`, `handle location invoke applies authorization required by mode`). canvas.present is covered by the app run above rather than the unit test, because on main it would open a real canvas window in the test process.

Checks: pinned swiftlint 0.65.1 `--strict` and swiftformat 0.63.1 `--lint` are clean on both files, and `git diff --check` is clean.

Production delta +27/-19; test delta +33/-0.

Merge risk: two-way door. Reverting restores the old behavior with no state or config migration. Blast radius is raw `node.invoke` calls to the five macOS commands whose params do not decode.

This issue is labeled `impact:security`. The change only narrows behavior: it rejects requests main executed with defaults and keeps the existing OpenClaw and OS permission checks unchanged.
